                "@xml:lang": "en"
              },
              {
                "#text": "生产混合，在工厂",
                "@xml:lang": "zh"
              }
            ],
            "treatmentStandardsRoutes": []
          },
          "comments": [
            {
              "#text": "Indigo is a deep color close to the color wheel blue, based on the ancient dye of the same name. The dye was originally exported to Europe from India. It used to be a natural dye made from Indigofera shrubs. The naturally occurring precursor of indigo is indican, a colourless, water-soluble substance that is easily hydrolyzed to glucose and indoxyl; the latter is converted to indigo by mild oxidation, such as exposure to air.",
              "@xml:lang": "en"
            },
            {
              "#text": "靛蓝是一种接近色轮蓝的深色，以古代同名染料为基础。这种染料最初从印度出口到欧洲。它曾经是一种由 Indigofera 灌木制成的天然染料。靛蓝的天然前体是茚满，它是一种无色的水溶性物质，很容易水解为葡萄糖和茚满酮；后者在轻度氧化（如暴露在空气中）后转化为靛蓝。",
              "@xml:lang": "zh"
            }
          ],
          "CAS": "482-89-3",
          "classification": {
            "common:classification": {
              "common:class": [
                {
                  "#text": "Other transportable goods, except metal products, machinery and equipment",
                  "@level": "0",
                  "@classId": "3"
                },
                {
                  "#text": "Basic chemicals",
                  "@level": "1",
                  "@classId": "34"
                },
                {
                  "#text": "Tanning or dyeing extracts; tannins and their derivatives; colouring matter n.e.c.",
                  "@level": "2",
                  "@classId": "343"
                },
                {
                  "#text": "Tanning extracts of vegetable origin; tannins and their salts, ethers, esters and other derivatives; colouring matter of vegetable or animal origin, except animal black; preparations based on colouring matter of vegetable or animal origin",
                  "@level": "3",
                  "@classId": "3432"
